      {
        "text": "Information Technology",
        "title": "Critical Infrastructure Sectors",
        "category": "other"
      },
      {
        "text": "The U.S. Government Accountability Office (GAO) Electronic Protest Docketing System (EPDS) and Civilian Board of Contract Appeals (CBCA) Electronic Docketing System (EDS) contained multiple vulnerabilities. In the worst case, a remote, unauthenticated attacker could change all users' passwords and gain administrative privileges.",
        "title": "Risk Evaluation",
        "category": "summary"
      },
      {
        "text": "These vulnerabilities were confirmed to be fixed as of 2026-03-19.",
        "title": "Recommended Practices",
        "category": "general"
      },
      {
        "text": "United States",
        "title": "Company Headquarters Location",
        "category": "other"
      }
    ],
